Z||000007||kempo||12-21-2001||11:42 PM||||I don't mean to flame anybody here, as I would much rather have a discussion with people about this topic.  <BR>You are correct in the statement that God gave us what we have, but I highly doubt that a 15 year old boy would be mature enough and mentally stable enough to engage in such an act, even though it was a dieing wish.  Just because you are dieing does not mean that you should be allowed to do such a thing.  <BR>Now I don't mean to say that I am the person here who says what people can and cannot do, but this is just a shocker.  <BR>By law, you are required to be at least the age of 18 to even look at pornographic material.  Granted this is a separate matter, no 15 year old should be doing what this child (yes, CHILD) has done.  What's worse is that his physcologist help set it up, and worse than that, they kept the truth from the childs own parents.<BR>How can you tell me that this is not messed up?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mach10||12-22-2001||03:36 AM||||2 schools of thought:<BR>1) the doctor has forgotten more than most of us will ever know... If HE says the kid's mentally equiped, it would stand up in court...<P>2) It was irresponsible to ENTERTAIN the notion. Why was it sent for evaluation? Props to the kid for getting some (  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> ), but it should not have had any such intervention. It's right, in that it WAS a dying wish (no matter how controversial... Remember that)... It falls SQUARELY in the "Grey" area.... <P>It's a real bad mix... However, the kid's gone, and was happy... I think that this is what should be focused on.||||reg||3
